75162>>>// This provides a quick and simple way to create an about package for a program.
75162>>>// You need to create a message inside you client area called Activate_About.
75162>>>// Within this message you should send the message DoAbout passing needed
75162>>>// string information.
75162>>>//
75162>>>//       Procedure Activate_About
75162>>>//           Send DoAbout sTitle sVersion sCopyright sAuthor sBitmap
75162>>>//       End_Procedure
75162>>>//    where: sTitle =     Name of application. If none provided, uses caption
75162>>>//                        bar title
75162>>>//           sVersion   = Version Line. If none provided, will be blank
75162>>>//           sCopyRight = Copyright Line. If none provided, will be blank
75162>>>//           sAuthor    = Author name, blank if none provided
75162>>>//           sBitMap    = Bitmap logo. If none provided, standard VDF bitmap
75162>>>//                        is used.
75162>>>// It is expected that you will place this in your own object package. For
75162>>>// example an order about package may look like this:
75162>>>//
75162>>>//   // OrderAbout.pkg
75162>>>//   Use StdAbout.pkg
75162>>>//   Procedure Activate_About
75162>>>//      String sTitle sCopyright sVersion sAuthor
75162>>>//      Move "My Order Entry System" to sTitle
75162>>>//      Move "Version 2.1" to sVersion
75162>>>//      Move "Copyright xxxx, Super Software Inc." to sCopyright
75162>>>//      Move "John Smith"  to sAuthor
75162>>>//      Send DoAbout sTitle sVersion sCopyright sAuthor ""
75162>>>//   end_procedure
75162>>>//   // end of file.
